const e="festival-vina-del-mar-chile",l=2027,t="Read both official English rule documents for the 66th Festival 2027 (International Genre and Folkloric Genre; 17-page notarised scans, 7 sheets each, read page by page) and the municipality news page of 10 July 2026. The two documents are almost the same text, so shared rules sit in Page.Sections and only the differences are on the two competition rows (folk definition, the 1-page folk justification, the live musician, 4 vs 3 vocal members, accommodation for 4 vs 3). Placed: purpose, invitation, six songs per competition, country rule, song conditions, registration steps, documents and technical formats, selection commission, mix of foreign and Chilean songs, orchestration deadlines, performer rules, performance conduct, fines, rights, stay, food, travel and insurance, jury, voting, prizes, acceptance, complaints, contact and definitions. Edition facts are Variables: apply dates and time, festival dates, venue, age cut-off, selection and results dates, orchestration deadline, both prizes, contact email, news. The rules do NOT print: any entry fee, a street address of Quinta Vergara, points or grade bands (only the 1 to 7 rating scale is printed, placed under Jury and Voting), prizes beyond the two awards, or any age groups or participant types. The template carries two groups called Comp Folclorica and Comp Internac with ages from 16, but the rules require the performer to be 18 by 30 November 2026; the rules' own wording is written and no AgeGroup row was added. The Folkloric rules still say 'International Competition' in the performance and rights sections, and give an interpreter as 3 members in the definitions but 4 vocal members in the interpreters rule; both are written as printed. Section numbers in the PDFs repeat (two sections 11), so rows cite the heading text. The Spanish text prevails over the English text.",o=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"66th Vina del Mar International Song Festival 2027: Folk and International song competitions. Read these rules before you apply.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"Applications are sent only through the online form {{ApplicationForm}} from {{RegistrationOpens}} to {{RegistrationDeadline}} at {{RegistrationDeadlineTime}}. The festival is held from {{FestivalStartDate}} to {{FestivalEndDate}} at {{Venue}}. Questions: {{ApplicantsContact}}.","Notes":["The rules are written in Spanish. If the English and Spanish texts differ, the Spanish text is the one that counts.","The festival production can change any deadline at any time without notice. News is given through the media it chooses.","Applications sent to BIZARRO, MEGAMEDIA or the Municipalidad of Vina del Mar are not accepted."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["The Promotion Committee of the 66th Festival of Vina del Mar holds two music competitions: the International Genre competition and the Folkloric Genre competition. Both take place in the amphitheater of Quinta Vergara in Vina del Mar, Chile.","The goal of the festival is to promote popular music worldwide. It is a place to show and recognise every author, composer and emerging performer with outstanding work, and it recognises Chilean and international music and cultural exchange between the countries taking part.","Chilean and foreign authors, composers and performers are invited to take part in the selection of the foreign and Chilean songs.","The rules are published on the websites www.elfestival.tv and www.munivina.cl and are announced through record companies in Chile. For foreign countries a press release goes with the rules to media, authors' societies and music labels on the five continents, through authors' societies, embassies and consulates of Chile abroad, and through advertising on MEGAMEDIA screens and international broadcasters.","In each competition six songs take part: five foreign songs (only one song per country) and one song that represents Chile.","Special places may be kept for countries whose song is chosen through a foreign television programme or a special scouting call, or through special invitations. If such a programme is held, it is the only way for people of that country to be chosen. The Chilean song can also be chosen through a Chilean television programme, and then the Chilean song is chosen only through that programme.","The country a song represents is the nationality of the author of the song. If the lyrics have more than one author, the applicants must give the nationality of one of them in the registration form. The nationality of the performer is not used to decide the country.","The festival production and the elected Commission are the only bodies that make sure these rules are followed.","The rules, their later changes, the decisions of the Commission and the festival production, and the verdicts of the jury are accepted by everyone who takes part. Participants give up any appeal against them, and must stay in the competition to the end.","Chosen participants must, if the festival production asks, sign a participation agreement. Its terms can add to or change the conditions in these rules to meet the organising or artistic needs of the festival.","Any doubt about how the rules are used or understood is settled by the production of the 2027 festival.","Applicants accept that nothing in their performances infringes copyright or related rights of other people. The applicant agrees to keep the production, BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA free of all costs, including legal defence, if anyone starts a legal action against the organisers or the Municipalidad because of such acts.","By taking part, applicants and chosen candidates accept that the performance is recorded, sold, broadcast and re-broadcast live or later, in Chile and abroad, on free television, limited television, international signals, IP signals and other media, including the internet, mobile phones, tablets, VOD and SmartTV, through channels that BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA choose, without any limit.","The competitors allow BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA to record, copy, produce and sell sound and audiovisual copies of the performances, and to use sound and audiovisual products with these performances in Chile and abroad, for promotion and for business, with the widest legal protection.","Registration in the competition is enough permission from the holders of the rights in the song for it to be used under these rules.","BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA may sell, together or separately and for their own benefit, the presentation of the applicants and competitors at the festival.","BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA still have to pay royalties to the body that represents the copyright and related rights, where it applies.","Definitions: the author wrote the original lyrics; the composer composed the original music; the applicant sent the registration form and fully accepted the conditions; the interpreter is the person who sings the song (vocalist); competitors or participants are the group of interpreters, authors and composers."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["The song must not have taken part in any international or national festival before 22 February 2027.","The song must be no longer than 3 minutes (180 seconds).","The song must be no more than 5 years old, counted from the date it was registered with the rights management company or intellectual property registry. The registration date must be written in the documents sent at the time of registration.","The song must be original. It must not be copied or be in a copyright dispute or any other legal dispute that could limit any right.","Songs licensed for use in public synchronisation or mass media are not eligible.","An author, composer or performer may send at most two songs. All must be for one category only, international or folk, and only one of them can be pre-selected.","Officials or employees of BIZARRO, MEGAMEDIA, their associated media and the Municipalidad of Vina del Mar, their spouses, and their relatives up to the fourth degree by blood or marriage, cannot take part.","The performer is the person who sings the song (the vocalist). The performer must be at least 18 years old on {{AgeCutoffDate}}.","The performer can be a well-known singer or an emerging figure.","Performers can be vocalists and instrumentalists.","All performers must be named in the registration form. Only they are allowed on the stage.","Any breach of these requirements means the song is disqualified. The festival organisation, with the Commission, may then choose another participant who followed the rules, at its own choice and at any time."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Apply","Items":["Registration is for songs. Authors, composers and performers who want to take part register their songs.","Send the application and all the documents below through the online form at {{ApplicationForm}}. A QR code to the form is also shown in promotions and programmes of MEGAMEDIA and its associated media.","Applications are received from {{RegistrationOpens}} to {{RegistrationDeadline}} at {{RegistrationDeadlineTime}}.","Each Chilean or foreign author, composer or performer must include a YouTube link (hidden) to a video of the performer or group performing the song. It can be an official music video or a recording made for this application. BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA may spread this video in any media they choose to promote the festival. Taking part means accepting this.","If the author or composer has died, the person presenting the work must bring a document signed before a Notary Public or Minister of Similar Faith, in the place where it is made, by the members of the estate or by whoever represents the rights. It must allow the use of the work.","Include a document that proves the song is registered in the Intellectual Property Registry or in the authors' society of the country it represents. It must name the author and the composer.","If the song is not presented by its original author or composer, the person who registers must show the permission given before a notary or a competent Minister of Faith. It must cover use of the work by third parties, including the performance at the festival, the permissions in the rights section of these rules, and any other use in these rules.","Attach a copy of the lyrics. It must show the title of the song, the performer or group, the country and the genre (folk or international). If the song is in a language other than Spanish, a translation into Spanish must also be sent.","Attach a copy of the master recording. It must be made to the technical standards of professional recording that allow commercial phonographic reproduction. BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA keep the right to use the powers in the rights section of these rules.","Recordings must be of high professional quality, made in a professional studio with good mixing and mastering, with clear, balanced sound without distortion, in Wav 48/24, Wav 44/16 or MP3 320 format.","Write a short biography of the author, composer and performer in the space given in the online form.","Attach promotional photographs in high resolution in jpg format. At least 3 colour photographs of the performer or group are needed.","Applicants who do not meet all the requirements are left out of the song submission process.","The festival production decides whether to tell applicants the result of the selection. Chosen applicants are told by email at the address given in the application form."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"Selection","Items":["A Song Selection Commission chooses the songs. It has a representative of the Chilean Society of National Authors and Performers (SCD), a member of the Municipalidad of Vina del Mar, a professional representative of the Chilean music industry, a prominent national author, composer or musician, and a musical director of the festival. The Commission for the Promotion of the 66th Festival appoints the members.","BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA, with the Municipalidad, may appoint more members. Each must be one of: a representative of an international organisation of high standing in the music industry; a prominent journalist, music critic or representative of a national media; an outstanding national or international musician or academic.","The Commission chooses, at its own judgement, the songs that fully meet the requirements. Only one song per country may be chosen.","The mix of the pre-selection jury is set by agreement between BIZARRO, MEGAMEDIA and the Municipalidad of Vina del Mar, under the general administrative and technical rules of the festival.","Foreign songs: the Commission names the five countries from all the songs that come from the call or by invitation. If countries are chosen through a foreign television programme, the Commission names only the places still missing.","Chilean song: the Commission names the song that represents Chile, except when a television programme is held to choose it. Then the Commission does not choose the Chilean song.","The selection takes place in {{SelectionWeek}}. Results are published in the week after the selection, starting {{ResultsDate}}.","From the moment a song is chosen and until the festival is over, the chosen performers cannot record or take part in interviews, programmes, recitals or other mass musical activities in the Republic of Chile."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Performers and Musicians","Items":["Only the performers named in the registration form may go on the stage.","A performer named in the registration form cannot be replaced without written permission from the Commission.","The group must choose one person to be the contact between the group or performer and the festival production. This person must be named in the registration form.","Chosen Chilean and foreign competitors must send the instrumentation or orchestration needed for the song to the festival production, with the multitrack or STEMS of the song in WAV format. The time to tell the production starts three days after the songs are chosen and ends on {{OrchestrationDeadline}}.","Selected songs are performed live with the orchestra led by the music director of the festival. Composers and authors have until {{OrchestrationDeadline}} to give the orchestral arrangements to the production.","If the competitor needs an instrument that is not in the standard orchestra, it can be added as an exception with the prior approval of the production. The competitor pays all costs of this, and of any performing musician who is not in the registration form. The production may accept or refuse such a request for the good of the competition.","Each performer may use a supporting musical sequence of professional quality with the final version of the song, in the week of the competition. The festival production alone decides if it is used."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Performance and Conduct","Items":["Each song is performed live on the stage of Quinta Vergara at least twice during the festival.","Songs are sung live in the language in which the author wrote them. This need not be the official language of the performer's country.","Each song is performed without breaks or changes, in line with the lyrics sent with the application. The performer and the accompanists must not change the melody or the lyrics for any reason. If they do, the production can disqualify the song at once.","Competitors must accept the staging set by the festival production for each of their presentations. The production will try to make the staging a good match for the song.","The festival production sets the dates and times of each presentation on the Quinta Vergara stage, using technical and artistic criteria.","Chosen competitors must take part in all promotional activities the production names, such as BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA programmes, notes, docureality programmes, recordings of rehearsals and interviews. All activity can be recorded and the rights are held by BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA.","Chosen competitors cannot take part in any other television programme in Chile without prior permission from the production. They cannot take part in public or private events outside the festival production in the week, or in the days, before it.","A performer who refuses to take part in the promotional activities can be fined up to 500 monthly tax units (UTM). A selected party who stops taking part without a good reason, after being qualified by BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA, can be made to pay back all costs of the performer and musicians and a fine of up to 1,000 monthly tax units, as an advance estimate of the damage. Fines must be paid within the first 30 days after BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA tell the party of the breach.","The production may stop at any time any performance that breaks these rules. The participant gives up any pay, compensation or indemnity for this.","If the rules are broken, the performers must pay back to BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA the full amount of the costs of their taking part."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Jury and Voting","Items":["A Commission of representatives of the Municipalidad of Vina del Mar, BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA appoints the same jury for the International and the Folkloric competitions.","The jury has at most 9 people, plus a possible virtual jury set through a web application or another technology service. Together they decide the winning songs at Quinta Vergara.","Jury members vote through an electronic system. The ratings are known at once to the public in Quinta Vergara and to the artists.","There may be one or more hidden scores from a set jury that can change each day. Hidden scores are not averaged with the rest and give a partial average. At the end of the phase, the results go to the presenters under notarial certification from the three qualified countries.","The final vote is certified by a Notary Public.","Each jury member rates the artists between 1 and 7 during the broadcast, and may include a relevant decimal.","In each competition, only the three songs with the best averages from the jury ratings, among the six songs, are presented in the final. They are scored live by the jury with the electronic voting system.","The song with the best average rating on the final night of the competition is the winner.","If there is a tie, in choosing the finalists or in the final, the President of the Jury and two jurors named on the first day of the festival decide in the same act, in a separate meeting, who the selected participants or the winner will be.","The decisions and ratings of the jury cannot be challenged by participants or by third parties."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Awards","Items":["Two prizes are given in each competition: the Winning Song Award and the Best Performer Award.","Winning Song Award: the author or authors and the composer or composers of the winning song receive a total gross prize of {{WinningSongPrize}}, paid in its money equivalent, with the Silver Seagull Award (Gaviota de Plata), the official symbol of the festival prize.","If BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA must pay any tax on sending the prize abroad, the tax is taken from the prize. The winner gets the money equivalent of the prize less any tax of the recipient's country.","If the author or composer is not at the venue, the Silver Seagull Award is given to the performer of the winning song. The performer must then give the award and the prize money to the author, or to the heirs if the author has died.","Best Performer Award: the performer or performers chosen as Best Performer receive a total gross prize of {{BestPerformerPrize}}. The winner gets the money equivalent less all taxes, including those of Chile and of the country where the winner lives, with the Silver Seagull Award (Gaviota de Plata).","Prize money is paid within the first 20 business days after the 2027 festival ends, in the form and currency that BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA decide. It is worked out with the Observed Exchange Rate (Tipo de Cambio Observado) of the Central Bank of Chile on the day of payment.","The organisers take no responsibility for any tax on the prizes. Each winner alone pays the taxes due under the laws of his or her country of residence and any other law that applies. The festival production may keep back any amount that the law requires.","Only one award is given to an interpreter group."]},{"Key":"payments","Title":"Stay, Food and Travel for Chosen Participants","Items":["Chosen participants receive from the organisation: stay, food and transport, as below. No pay or fee for performing is printed in the rules.","Accommodation: in the place and rooms set by the festival production, for up to 15 days in February 2027, from a date set by BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA. Phone calls, minibar, room service, laundry, ironing and similar services are not included.","Accommodation is also given for one more person, who can only be a manager, composer or author. This person must be named in the registration form and is chosen by the performers, under the conditions set by BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA. The person may share the room with the performer.","Food is given to the performers and one companion (manager, author or composer), in a place set by the production, for the length of the contest and up to 15 days in February 2027. Extra items such as alcohol or anything outside the standard food service are not included.","Each foreign interpreter named in the registration form and chosen by the Commission receives an economy class return ticket between the country of origin and Santiago de Chile. The production decides the airline or other transport. The production pays boarding fees or taxes that are not in the ticket of artists from abroad.","Taxes for leaving their own country (including visas) and charges for overweight luggage, going and returning, are paid by the competitors.","The production organises and pays the ground transport of performers and companions between Santiago de Chile, Vina del Mar and Santiago de Chile, and inside Vina del Mar for the activities of the competition.","A Chilean competitor is moved from the city of residence to Vina del Mar by airline or other transport that the production decides.","After artists accept the tickets and itinerary, any change of date or name on the tickets or airline that the competitors ask for is charged to them and must be made through their own management.","Transport is also given, on the same terms, for one more person: a manager, author or composer chosen by the performers. If the manager lives in Chile, the transfer is given inside Chile.","The production gives no free or courtesy tickets to participants chosen for the competition.","The festival has a permanent first aid service. If a major medical emergency happens at the event, at the venue or elsewhere, the organisation does not pay the medical and hospital costs of the performers.","The interpreter and companions must have international health insurance taken in their own country before the trip to Chile. The proof must be sent to the organisation within 30 days after BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA tell the participant that he or she is chosen.","BIZARRO and MEGAMEDIA do not give credentials, accommodation, food or tickets to any other companion than those in the stay and transport rules, nor to authors, composers or orchestra directors. Credentials are given by the organisation and are only for those registered on the form as singers, plus a representative, manager or author."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Complaints and Appeals","Items":["All decisions of the elected Commission and the festival production about the organisation of the event, and those of the jury about the performance and choice of the winning songs, are final. No appeal or administrative claim is allowed.","A claim by any person or body about the intellectual property of the songs, or about a breach of these rules, must be sent in writing to the Executive Secretary of the Festival Promotion Commission up to 30 working days before the festival begins. It must come with evidence that clearly shows that an irregularity or plagiarism has happened. The festival production may rule up to 10 days before the festival starts.","Questions about the rules, the application or the running of the competition go to {{ApplicantsContact}}."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Bases for the Festival 2027 (all four documents)","Url":"https://www.munivina.cl/bases-festival-de-la-cancion-vina-del-mar-2027/"},{"Title":"International Genre Rules (English)","Url":"https://www.munivina.cl/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/BASES-COMPETENCIA-INTERNACIONAL-version-ingles.pdf"},{"Title":"Folkloric Genre Rules (English)","Url":"https://www.munivina.cl/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/BASES-COMPETENCIA-FOLCLORICA-version-Ingles.pdf"},{"Title":"Bases Competencia Internacional (Spanish, the text that counts)","Url":"https://www.munivina.cl/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/BASES-COMPETENCIA-INTERNACIONAL.pdf"},{"Title":"Bases Competencia Folclorica (Spanish, the text that counts)","Url":"https://www.munivina.cl/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/BASES-COMPETENCIA-FOLCLORICA.pdf"},{"Title":"Online application form","Url":"https://elfestival.tv/competencias"}]}`),n=[],a=[],i=[{Title:"Cancion - Competencia Internacional (International Song)",Source:"International Genre Rules (English version, 17-page notarised PDF), sections 7.4, 10.1, 11.2 and 13",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Performers may have at most three vocal members, not choirs. Musicians are not counted.","Accommodation is for the performers, up to 3 people, plus one more person (manager, composer or author).","In the definitions of the same document, an interpreter cannot be more than 3 members."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:["The song with the best average rating on the final night of the International Competition is the winner."],Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Performers may have at most three vocal members, not choirs. Musicians are not counted.
- Accommodation is for the performers, up to 3 people, plus one more person (manager, composer or author).
- In the definitions of the same document, an interpreter cannot be more than 3 members.

## Judging
- The song with the best average rating on the final night of the International Competition is the winner.`},{Title:"Cancion - Competencia Folclorica (Folk Song)",Source:"Folkloric Genre Rules (English version, 17-page notarised PDF), sections 3.1, 4.3 (i), 6.2, 7.4, 10.1, 11.2 and 13",Sections:{About:["A folk song is any musical work that represents or is inspired by popular-rooted musical expressions of a community, territory or country. This can show in its rhythm, musical form, lyrics, instrumentation or themes.","Songs with contemporary production or modern stylistic fusions are also accepted if they keep a clear and substantial link to the folklore of the country or region they represent.","Such hybrid songs must show respect for, and inspiration from, musical traditions, in an explicit or conceptual way."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["With the application, attach a short document of at most 1 page that explains why the song is a folk work. It must give the cultural or geographical context of the song, the stylistic elements (rhythms, scales, themes, traditional forms), the musical references that inspired it, and the artist's intent about its folklore roots or identity.","Each performance must include at least one musician playing live on stage with an acoustic instrument or one that is typical of folklore.","Performers may have at most four vocal members, not choirs. Musicians are not counted.","Accommodation is for the performers, up to 4 people, plus one more person (manager, composer or author).","In the definitions of the same document, an interpreter cannot be more than 3 members. This differs from the limit of four in the interpreters rule."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:["The song with the best average rating on the final night of the Folkloric Competition is the winner."],Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- A folk song is any musical work that represents or is inspired by popular-rooted musical expressions of a community, territory or country. This can show in its rhythm, musical form, lyrics, instrumentation or themes.
- Songs with contemporary production or modern stylistic fusions are also accepted if they keep a clear and substantial link to the folklore of the country or region they represent.
- Such hybrid songs must show respect for, and inspiration from, musical traditions, in an explicit or conceptual way.

## Rules
- With the application, attach a short document of at most 1 page that explains why the song is a folk work. It must give the cultural or geographical context of the song, the stylistic elements (rhythms, scales, themes, traditional forms), the musical references that inspired it, and the artist's intent about its folklore roots or identity.
- Each performance must include at least one musician playing live on stage with an acoustic instrument or one that is typical of folklore.
- Performers may have at most four vocal members, not choirs. Musicians are not counted.
- Accommodation is for the performers, up to 4 people, plus one more person (manager, composer or author).
- In the definitions of the same document, an interpreter cannot be more than 3 members. This differs from the limit of four in the interpreters rule.

## Judging
- The song with the best average rating on the final night of the Folkloric Competition is the winner.`}],r=[],s=[{Key:"ApplicationForm",Kind:"link",Label:"Online application form",Value:"https://elfestival.tv/competencias",Source:"Rules section 4.1 (both genres)"},{Key:"RegistrationOpens",Kind:"date",Label:"First day to apply",Value:"2026-07-16",Source:"Rules section 4.2 (Thursday, July 16, 2026)"},{Key:"RegistrationDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to apply",Value:"2026-09-25",Source:"Rules section 4.2 (Friday, September 25, 2026)"},{Key:"RegistrationDeadlineTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Time on the last date",Value:"18:00 (Chile time)",Source:"Rules section 4.2 (18:00 p.m. in Chile)"},{Key:"FestivalStartDate",Kind:"date",Label:"First day of the festival",Value:"2027-02-22",Source:"Rules opening paragraph"},{Key:"FestivalEndDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Last day of the festival",Value:"2027-02-27",Source:"Rules opening paragraph"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Event venue",Value:{Name:"Quinta Vergara amphitheater",Address:"",City:"Vina del Mar, Chile",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Rules opening paragraph (street address not printed)"},{Key:"AgeCutoffDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Date by which the performer must be 18",Value:"2026-11-30",Source:"Rules section 7.1"},{Key:"SelectionWeek",Kind:"text",Label:"When the songs are selected",Value:"the third week of October 2026",Source:"Rules section 5.1"},{Key:"ResultsDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Start of the week when results are published",Value:"2026-10-22",Source:"Rules section 5.1 (week following the selection, beginning October 22, 2026)"},{Key:"OrchestrationDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to send orchestration and arrangements",Value:"2026-11-30",Source:"Rules, musical accompaniment section (November 30, 2026)"},{Key:"WinningSongPrize",Kind:"prize",Label:"Winning Song Award",Value:"UF 739 (seven hundred thirty-nine Unidades de Fomento), gross, with the Silver Seagull (Gaviota de Plata)",Source:"Rules section 11.3 (a)"},{Key:"BestPerformerPrize",Kind:"prize",Label:"Best Performer Award",Value:"UF 246 (two hundred forty-six Unidades de Fomento), gross, with the Silver Seagull (Gaviota de Plata)",Source:"Rules section 11.3 (b)"},{Key:"ApplicantsContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Email for questions about the rules and the application",Value:{Name:"Applicants enquiries (Competencias)",Role:"Festival production",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"postulantes.competencias@elfestival.tv"},Source:"Rules section 12 (Others)"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"News printed by the organiser",Value:[{Date:"2026-07-10",Title:"Rules for the Folk and International competitions are published",Text:"The municipality of Vina del Mar, with Megamedia and Bizarro, published the rules for the 66th festival (22 to 27 February 2027). Six songs are chosen for each competition: five foreign and one Chilean, each at most 3 minutes and registered no more than five years ago. Folk songs may include contemporary elements if they keep a real link to the traditions of their territory, need a short document explaining their cultural roots, and each performance needs at least one live musician with an acoustic or typical folklore instrument. Formal applications start on 16 July 2026.",Url:"https://www.munivina.cl/noticias/comienza-la-carrera-por-la-gaviota-de-plata-vina-2027-entrega-las-bases-de-las-competencias-internacional-y-folclorica/"}],Source:"Municipalidad de Vina del Mar news page, 10 July 2026"}],h=[{Claim:"Rules, requirements, registration steps, dates, selection, performance, stay, jury, prizes and contact are those of the 66th Festival 2027 International Genre Rules (English version, notarised 8 July 2026).",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own rules document",Source:"Municipalidad de Vina del Mar, Bases Competencia Internacional, version ingles (17 pages, notarised)",Url:"https://www.munivina.cl/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/BASES-COMPETENCIA-INTERNACIONAL-version-ingles.pdf"},{Claim:"The Folk competition differences (folk definition, justification document, live musician, 4 vocal members, 4 people in accommodation) are those of the Folkloric Genre Rules (English version, notarised 8 July 2026).",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own rules document",Source:"Municipalidad de Vina del Mar, Bases Competencia Folclorica, version ingles (17 pages, notarised)",Url:"https://www.munivina.cl/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/BASES-COMPETENCIA-FOLCLORICA-version-Ingles.pdf"},{Claim:"The news item and the dates of the 2027 call are from the municipality's own news page.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own announcement",Source:"Municipalidad de Vina del Mar news, 10 July 2026",Url:"https://www.munivina.cl/noticias/comienza-la-carrera-por-la-gaviota-de-plata-vina-2027-entrega-las-bases-de-las-competencias-internacional-y-folclorica/"}],c={TemplateKey:e,Year:2027,Note:t,Page:o,ParticipantTypes:n,AgeGroups:a,Competitions:i,CompetitionAgeGroups:r,Variables:s,Evidence:h};export{a as AgeGroups,r as CompetitionAgeGroups,i as Competitions,h as Evidence,t as Note,o as Page,n as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,s as Variables,l as Year,c as default};
